{"action_id":"action.6d6f0cf27ba3440ea7c3c1d0ba99531a","provenance":{"allowance_slot":25,"cli_version":"codex-cli 0.153.4","configuration":"ignore-user-config; read-only; tools-disabled; no-resume","events_jsonl":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0ccf1-28c6-7420-bea5-b607bf7845d4\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"coverage\\\": [\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"States the extended parallel run and compulsory route from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Background heading; no independent condition.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u2\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Provides launch history, WINGS context and examples of application/submission types; the earlier circular is not supplied.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u3\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the parallel run, read with its extension.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Section heading linking extension and enhancements.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u5\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Describes monitoring and feedback; adds no submission condition.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u6\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Confirms the revised parallel-run endpoint; enhancement rationale does not expressly condition commencement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Full-adoption heading supports the compulsory-route context.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u8\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Restates the compulsory route, describes integration of reporting requests and separately permits fee settlement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Enquiries heading; no independent route requirement.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u10\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Operational review and contact guidance; practicability qualifies enhancements, not compulsory submission.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the issuing division.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u12\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the issuing commission.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u13\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Document-end marker.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u14\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies product categories associated with the IPD scope; exhaustiveness remains unresolved.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Expands WINGS; does not create a separate route obligation.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u18\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The control attaches to applications and submissions concerning investment products administered by IPD and submitted to IPD. It governs the submitting actor in that capacity; it does not impose an institution-wide or bank-specific duty.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"IPD and e-IP are identified, and WINGS is expanded. The footnote lists product categories without expressly saying whether the list exhausts IPD-administered products. Applications and submissions are not comprehensively defined.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\",\\\"u18\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"exceptions\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Existing-channel acceptance attaches to the parallel run, whose endpoint is extended. No post-transition exception or grandfathering rule is stated. The practicability qualification concerns operational enhancement.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"modality\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Must establishes the compulsory submission route. Can also makes annual-fee settlement an available facility. Statements that features will be introduced and requests will be integrated do not themselves create new reporting or payment duties.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u11\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The revised parallel run ends on 29 November 2024 and the compulsory route begins on 30 November 2024, inclusively. The original 29 October endpoint is superseded. Treatment of later correspondence in pre-transition cases is not expressly addressed.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"PROPOSED\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"dimension\\\":\\\"dependencies\\\",\\n      \\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The earlier launch circular and the packet's external-authorities.24ec50 dependency are unavailable. They may clarify product classification, existing channels and migration procedures. The supplied text states a fixed commencement date without making it contingent on enhancement completion.\\\",\\n      \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u4\\\",\\\"u7\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n      \\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Is the product list in footnote 1 exhaustive, or does IPD administration independently determine coverage?\\\",\\n    \\\"Does the earlier circular provide special handling for follow-up submissions in cases opened through existing channels before 30 November 2024?\\\",\\n    \\\"What do the unavailable launch circular and external-authorities.24ec50 dependency specify about submission classification and migration procedures?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"readings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\n        \\\"The assessment concerns one identified submission event, not whole-institution compliance or whether an underlying filing is due.\\\",\\n        \\\"Extending the parallel run carries forward its existing-channel acceptance through 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n        \\\"The event's submission date determines application of the compulsory route; no unstated grandfathering exception is inserted.\\\",\\n        \\\"Product and submission classification remain supplied facts requiring judgment where the retained text is insufficient.\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"citations\\\":[\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"After the extended period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by the Investment Products Division (IPD)1 must be submitted to IPD via e-IP from 30 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u1\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u4\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"To facilitate these enhancements, the SFC will extend the parallel run period of e-IP by one month to 29 November 2024.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u7\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u9\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"1 Investment-linked assurance schemes, mandatory provident fund products, open-ended fund companies, paper gold schemes, pooled retirement funds, real estate investment trusts, unit trusts and mutual funds and unlisted structured investment products.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u17\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"quote\\\":\\\"The SFC will continue to review and enhance the operation of e-IP where practicable.\\\",\\n          \\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"u11\\\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \\\"distinction\\\":\\\"This reading applies the transition to each covered submission event, including later submissions relating to an earlier case where they otherwise qualify. It preserves optional fee settlement and treats enhancement completion as rationale rather than a commencement condition. The strongest uncertainty is whether unavailable migration provisions qualify the treatment of existing cases; the retained text supplies insufficient support for a separate grandfathering reading.\\\",\\n      \\\"family\\\":\\\"time\\\",\\n      \\\"formalization\\\":{\\n        \\\"facts\\\":[\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed event is an application or submission to IPD concerning an investment product administered by IPD. Classification takes account of footnote 1 and does not classify use of the optional annual-fee facility alone as a covered submission.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"covered_submission\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":true,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u3\\\",\\\"u9\\\",\\\"u17\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date on which the assessed application or submission is made to IPD.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submission_date\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"date\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Gregorian calendar date\\\"\\n          },\\n          {\\n            \\\"meaning\\\":\\\"The assessed application or submission is submitted to IPD via e-IP.\\\",\\n            \\\"name\\\":\\\"submitted_via_eip\\\",\\n            \\\"requires_judgment\\\":false,\\n            \\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"u1\\\",\\\"u9\\\"],\\n            \\\"type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n            \\\"unit\\\":\\\"Boolean\\\"\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"result\\\":\\\"submitted_via_eip\\\",\\n        \\\"result_type\\\":\\\"bool\\\",\\n        \\\"scope\\\":\\\"(and covered_submission (>= submission_date (date 2024-11-30)))\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"local_id\\\":\\\"r1\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\":[\\n        \\\"For an existing case, which later communications count as applications or submissions subject to the new route?\\\",\\n        \\\"Does missing migration guidance provide any express exception to the event-date reading?\\\"\\n      ],\\n      \\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each covered application or submission made to IPD on or after 30 November 2024, the submitting actor must use e-IP. Existing channels remain accepted during the extended parallel run through 29 November 2024. The identified reporting requests fall within the integration described by the circular, without this text independently establishing when reports are due. Annual-fee settlement through e-IP remains optional. Within the formal scope, a true result means that this submission satisfies the selected route control; outside that scope, the formalization makes no compliance determination.\\\",\\n      \\\"subject\\\":\\\"Selected control: compulsory e-IP submission route and transition date\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":24588,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":2144,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":65}}\n","fresh_context":true,"independence":"CONTEXT_ONLY_SAME_MODEL_CORRELATION_UNMEASURED","model":"gpt-6-astra","provider":"codex.fresh.v1","provider_route_hash":"3d676052ff208f9c0b35467659af41d3138476127d0d1b523970689c2edf4714","request_hash":"71f265f67a6bbdcbd5e2d3647c4836cc3a8ae5193b78c750eb8348d5bde6187a","response_hash":"70e931cc40def82ef5e05426dce922652bacf70fee170930a2f6613031f8a10c","transport_retry_policy":"NO_APPLICATION_RETRY; CLI transport behavior is external","usage":[{"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"cached_input_tokens":0,"input_tokens":24588,"output_tokens":2144,"reasoning_output_tokens":65}],"wall_milliseconds":76188},"response":{"coverage":[{"reason":"States the extended parallel run and compulsory route from 30 November 2024.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading; no independent condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Provides launch history, WINGS context and examples of application/submission types; the earlier circular is not supplied.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Establishes acceptance of existing channels during the parallel run, read with its extension.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Section heading linking extension and enhancements.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Describes monitoring and feedback; adds no submission condition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Confirms the revised parallel-run endpoint; enh